          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="mono note">Where persistence across runs actually lives, October 2026. Deeper in the stack is lower on the list.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="c-a prose">
        <p class="mono reg">Measured · [28] · Press · [29]</p>
        <p>The software mirror: a 2026 paper formalizes session state kept across requests as a requirement for constant query latency, not an optimization <span class="cite">[28]</span>. NVIDIA announced a persistent, NVMe-resident KV cache as agentic long-term memory at CES 2026; press only, no patent located <span class="cite">[29]</span>.</p>
        <p class="mono reg">Position</p>
        <p class="beat">Nothing shipped in the weights. Everything shipped around them. That is the market telling you where the unsolved problem is.</p>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section n="05" title="The map" id="map">
      <div class="c-a prose">
        <p class="mono reg">Position</p>
        <p class="beat">What a lab publishes is what it is proud of. What it patents is what it sells.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="c-full field map">
        <div>
          <p class="mono-b">Published. No patent found.</p>
          <dl class="pairs">{published.map(([n, w]) => (<><dt>{n}</dt><dd class="mono">{w}</dd></>))}</dl>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="mono-b">Patented. No paper.</p>
          <dl class="pairs">{patented.map(([n, w]) => (<><dt>{n}</dt><dd class="mono">{w}</dd></>))}</dl>
        </div>
        <p class="mono note">What a lab publishes is what it is proud of. What it patents is what it sells. <span class="cite">[01] to [05], [08]</span></p>
      </div>
      <Stats class="c-b" items={[
        [String(published.length), 'Architectures published, no patent found'],
        [String(patented.length), 'Memory and state patents, no paper'],
        ['18', 'Months from filing to publication'],
      ]} />
      <div class="c-a prose">
        <p class="mono reg">Record · [30]</p>
        <p>The pattern holds outside the frontier labs. A Korean university filed a continual-learning method that learns only additive prompts on a frozen backbone to avoid forgetting; filed September 2025, published April 2026, no paper attached. Patent-only work is invisible to anyone who reads only arXiv.</p>
        <p class="mono reg">Measured</p>
        <p>No patent was located for Titans, Memory Layers, hyper-connections, attention sinks or registers. Applications publish eighteen months after filing. A Titans filing, if one exists, would not be visible yet. Absence of a record is not absence of a filing.</p>
        <p class="mono reg">Position</p>
        <p class="beat">Read the filings. They are the only place a lab tells you, under oath, what it thinks is worth owning.</p>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section n="05" title="The clock" ground="bottle" id="clock">
      <div class="c-a prose">
        <p class="mono reg">Record and measured</p>
        <p>Three clocks run at different speeds. Papers post within weeks of a result. Filings surface eighteen months after priority. Products ship when the business is ready, which is sometimes before the paper exists.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="c-full field scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Three clocks, 2021 to 2026">
        <table class="ledger clock">
          <caption class="sr">Papers, patents and products by year, 2021 to 2026.</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Year</th>{LANES.map((l) => (<th scope="col">{l}</th>))}</tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {years.map((y) => (<tr><th scope="row" class="mono-b">{y}</th>{LANES.map((l) => (<td>{cell(y, l)}</td>))}</tr>))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="mono note">A memory feature shipped before the first test-time memory paper was posted. The notepad beat the brain to market.</p>
      </div>
      <Stats class="c-b" items={[
        ['2024', 'ChatGPT Memory ships'],
        ['2025', 'First test-time memory paper, Titans [21]'],
        ['2026', 'Memory filing published [02]'],
      ]} />
      <div class="c-a prose">
        <p class="mono reg">Position</p>
        <p class="beat">ChatGPT Memory shipped in 2024. The first test-time memory paper posted in January 2025. The notepad beat the brain to market by most of a year, and the gap has not closed.</p>
        <p class="beat">If you want to know what persistence will look like in 2028, the filings of 2026 are the only forward-looking document that exists.</p>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section n="06" title="Where it is wrong" id="wrong">
      <div class="c-a prose">
        <p class="mono-b">06 · The case against</p>
      </div>
      <Rail items={[
        ['A', '<b>Absence of a patent is not absence of a filing.</b> Eighteen months of lag means every 2025 architecture filing is still dark. The map in section 05 is a map of what is visible, and the publish-versus-patent split could narrow in 2027 as filings surface.'],
        ['B', '<b>The four axes are my lens, not their taxonomy.</b> None of the cited papers uses the word persistence. Depth, tokens, time and runs is a synthesis. It organizes the material; it does not come from it. Treat it as a frame to argue with.'],
        ['C', '<b>The fourth axis may already be moving.</b> HOPE writes its own weights at inference [23]. Retrievable Gradients persist across runs without drift, outside the weights [26]. One published forgetting curve that stays flat across repeated updates ends this paper’s claim, and that paper could be in the NeurIPS 2026 camera-readies.'],
        ['D', '<b>A filing is a hedge, not a roadmap.</b> Companies patent defensively. A granted memory patent proves the mechanism was worth protecting, not that it is the mechanism in production today, and a product can change under a patent without a new filing.'],
      ]} />
      <Stats class="c-b" items={[
        ['0', 'Production models learning across runs in the weights'],
        ['3', 'Serious partial answers: HOPE, SEAL, Retrievable Gradients'],
        ['1', 'Flat forgetting curve would end the argument'],
      ]} />
    </Section>

    <Section n="07" title="Sources" id="sources">
