      <div class="c-a prose">
        <p class="mono reg">Colophon</p>
        <p>Set in Bricolage Grotesque and Martian Mono. The cover rose is computed from r = cos(kθ), frozen at k = 21/4, 37/5 and 19/6: a still from a film. Preprints dated 2026 are recent; open them before citing. Patent numbers from a patent analyst should be opened at the office record before they are repeated.</p>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section n="08" title="The axis" ground="bottle" id="axis">
      <div class="c-a prose">
        <p>A decade of architecture can be read as one project with three finished parts. The identity path taught a network to carry a signal through a hundred layers without losing it. Registers taught it to hold a thought that belongs to no token. State-space memory taught it to carry that thought across a million positions.</p>
        <p>Then the run ends, the state is discarded, and the next run starts from the photograph.</p>
        <p class="beat">Three axes are architecture. The fourth is still a product feature. Until a weight can learn on Tuesday and keep Monday, that is the whole business.</p>
      </div>
    </Section>

